Z||000000||wxxo||03-20-2000||06:00 PM|||| ok heres the deal. as soon as i turn the key and even before the motor starts on my 86 se v6 4spd the oil pressure gauge is pegged wayyyyyy past the high mark. any idea whats going on. hope its just a broken gauge.<BR>nothing strange going on with the car other than that. seems to ge running fine. help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||RICK||03-20-2000||06:50 PM||||Thats normal for the gauge to peg and then go to normal after the engine has started. There is a post somewhere (I couldn't find it) that shows how you can rewire it so it will not do this.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-20-2000||06:56 PM||||It's the water temp that normally pegs, not the oil.<P>try changing the oil sender.||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||03-20-2000||07:03 PM||||My quage did that 4 a while (about a week) then it started working like normal again.  Just now when I rev it it goes down to about 20 then stutters and shoots up to 80 and bounces around.  It stays at around 50 with cruise control on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||03-20-2000||08:15 PM||||Replace the oil sending unit and your problem will be cured.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||03-20-2000||08:40 PM||||NO, NO, NO, this is normal in all GM cars. It’s a self-test to let you know that the gauge is working. There is nothing wrong so don't go throwing parts at it. Just ignore it if it bothers you or write a nasty letter to General Motors. You should also notice the temp gauge dose this and all the idiot lights come on for a second to.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phaeton||03-20-2000||10:23 PM||||My Fiero kept eating oil senders until the harness was replaced, the weatherseal had deteriorated to where moisture got in, corroding contact surfaces on the pins.||||reg||1
Z||000007||wxxo||03-21-2000||12:43 PM||||got the problem fixed. thanks for all of the replys. turns out that the wire came loose. as much money as i have spent on that car they didnt charge me anything at the garage hahaha. its pretty bad when all of the mechanics know you by your first name hahaha. thanks again...||||reg||7
